   <li><strong>Network modeling, from regional to national.</strong> I began as a GIS analyst (Cross County Connection TMA), then a systems planner (Delaware Valley Regional Planning Commission) and a transportation consultant (IBI Group), building and running transportation network models. At the U.S. Federal Highway Administration I specified the national Tour-Based Model System for long-distance passenger travel and directed the contractor team that built it, co-directed the $10M National Household Travel Survey, and managed a $1.5M federal research portfolio as a certified Contracting Officer's Representative.</li>
   <li><strong>Data-driven decisions at national scale.</strong> At Deloitte I delivered analytics and machine-learning engagements for federal and public-sector clients. At AARP's Public Policy Institute I led the <a href="https://livabilityindex.aarp.org">Livability Index</a>, which combines 50+ data sources across 7 domains to score U.S. neighborhoods and inform policy decisions.</li>
   <li><strong>Autonomous systems research at <a href="https://qnfo.org">QNFO</a>.</strong> I designed and operate an autonomous AI research system that drafts, referees, revises, publishes and corrects papers. I treat it as a research object: what it delivers, what it costs, how it fails, and how its claims stay auditable.</li>
+  <li><strong>A self-governing development platform.</strong> The fleet behind QNFO has become a platform in its own right (working name Ultrastable). It finds its own work in its metrics and failures, hands each change to coding agents, proves every deploy live with an automatic rollback, and scores its decisions against the predictions it logged first: 3,880 merged changes since August 2026, and 73% of 1,056 scored decisions came out as predicted. QNFO is its first customer. <a href="https://github.com/QNFO/qnfo-workers/blob/main/docs/PRODUCT-ULTRASTABLE.md">What it is and where it falls short</a>.</li>
   <li><strong>Current questions:</strong> how do people keep oversight of autonomous AI systems that act on their own? How should such a system state what it does not know? What does a correct answer from an agentic system cost, in energy, for the whole system?</li>
 </ul>
 
